    78	    'Hivemind is a ledger of research views (a dated question with a five-step ladder, judged every day on evidence) '
    79	    'with a search engine on top. To read an idea against it: first break the idea into its parts, the one to four '
    80	    'questions whose answers decide it (each about one concrete quantity, date or event); search with the idea and with '
    81	    'each part (k=20); map each part to every view whose question answers it or whose outcome would move it, leaving out '
    82	    'views that only share a company or a word; then read each mapped view (state as of a day, history, evidence) and '
    83	    'say what the judged positions tell about each part and which parts no view covers. Say judged, never true. Every '
    84	    'tool takes as_of, a calendar day; the default is the ledger\'s last completed day. Nothing here changes the ledger. '
    85	    'search matches each view\'s own text (question, what it looks at, ladder conditions; Chinese, English queries work): '
    86	    'ask for one object and one quantity or event per query; views(object) lists everything under one object. '
    87	    + OBJECTS))
